**Technical Specification Document**  
**Project Title:** Advanced Genetic Engineering for Medical Device Development  
**Company:** BioGenTech Innovations, Inc.  
**Date:** October 15, 2023  
**Project Lead:** Dr. Emily Tran, PhD, Genetic Engineering Department  
**Location:** 4500 Research Park Drive, Suite 200, San Diego, CA 92121  
**Project Code:** BGT-MED-GEN-2023  

**1. Objective:**  
To develop a novel genetic engineering technique to enhance the efficacy of medical devices, specifically focusing on gene-editing tools such as CRISPR-Cas9, to improve patient outcomes in chronic diseases.

**2. Requirements:**  
- **Genetic Engineering Protocols:** Utilize CRISPR-Cas9 technology developed by the Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard (2014) to edit genes associated with diabetes and cardiovascular diseases.  
- **Device Integration:** Collaborate with MedDevices Corp. to integrate genetic modifications into their Implantable Glucose Monitor (IGM) system by Q4 2024.  
- **Regulatory Compliance:** Adhere to FDA guidelines for genetic modifications in medical devices as outlined in the 21 CFR Part 820.  
- **Clinical Trials:** Conduct trials in collaboration with Stanford University Medical Center, targeting at least 200 participants by 2025.

**3. Constraints:**  
- **Patents:** Ensure all genetic modifications are compliant with existing patents held by Editas Medicine, Inc. (US Patent No. 9,299,483) and CRISPR Therapeutics AG (US Patent No. 10,669,260).  
- **Budget Limitations:** Maintain project costs within a $5 million budget, funded through a grant from the National Institutes of Health (NIH) and private investment from BioVenture Partners.  
- **Timeline:** Complete initial research phase by March 2024, with device integration finalized by July 2025. Delays could incur penalties from stakeholders.

**4. Stakeholders:**  
- **Key Personnel:**  
  - Dr. Mark Chen, Lead Engineer at BioGenTech  
  - Dr. Laura Simmons, Clinical Trials Coordinator at Stanford University  
  - Dr. Raj Patel, Regulatory Affairs Specialist at MedDevices Corp.  
- **Collaborating Organizations:**  
  - University of California, San Diego (UCSD) for data analysis  
  - Genomic Health, Inc. for sequencing services  
